  "findings": [
    "Qwen3-Embedding-8B is the best local model, level with the best API model; Ollama's Q4_K_M scores as the FP8 served by an API",
    "the prefix matters, model by model: Qwen3-Embedding-8B scores 0.903 with the official instruction, 0.883 without one, 0.823 with one of ours; EmbeddingGemma drops from 0.856 to 0.809 without its prefix",
    "cutting the vector (Matryoshka) costs little: Qwen3-Embedding-8B from 4096 to 1024 numbers, 0.903 to 0.894 on scope D, 0.983 to 0.985 on Belebele",
    "a plain hybrid (BM25 and vectors with RRF, k = 60) lowers the strong models: Qwen3-Embedding-8B 0.983 to 0.932 on Belebele; it lifts only the weak ones"
  ],
  "choice": {
    "date": "2026-10-14",
    "what": "Qwen3-Embedding-8B on Ollama (Q4_K_M)",
    "why": "the best local model; it is about 8 times slower than EmbeddingGemma (an article of 256 chunks: about 28 s against 5 s), a cost paid once when documents are loaded"
  }
